/* Core-layer user-facing messages — English (default language). */

/* TransferFailureKind.message — what a failed transfer's typed cause
   renders to, one indirection below `TransferQueueViewModel.message(for:)`
   since 2026-09-25. The audit line writes it for every one of the fourteen
   causes (`AuditRecorder`); the App's transfer row reads it for eleven and
   says the other three itself (`TransferFailureLabel`), because
   `core.error.connectionLost %@` and `core.transfer.failed %@` are the two
   frames whose argument is a `reason` string rather than a path.

   Counted 2026-09-25: `core.transfer.failed %@` has 2 readers, both in
   `TransferFailureKind.message` (`protocolError`, `unknown`);
   `core.error.connectionLost %@` has 2 — that file's `connectionFailed`
   arm, and `RemoteBrowserViewModel.message(for:path:)`, which fills it
   with `DialSupport.reason(for:)` and is NOT one of the three the App
   takes over. What those arguments hold is mostly MacSCP's own English
   prose, not a server's words; see `TransferFailureLabel`'s doc comment
   for the measurement. */
"core.transfer.notFound %@" = "File not found: %@";
"core.error.permissionDenied %@" = "Permission denied for: %@";
"core.error.connectionLost %@" = "Connection lost: %@";
"core.transfer.failed %@" = "Transfer failed: %@";
"core.transfer.noFreeName" = "No available filename found.";
"core.transfer.interrupted" = "Connection lost — transfer interrupted.";
"core.transfer.connectionLost" = "Connection lost.";
